{"title":"2024 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 15","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Newton&#39;s_Sums_and_Vieta&#39;s)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Newton's Sums and Vieta's)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(Reduction_of_power)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (Reduction of power)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6_(Cheesing_it_out)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6 (Cheesing it out)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution,_Fast,_Quick,_Easy!\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution, Fast, Quick, Easy!</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_-_MaffyTaffy\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution - MaffyTaffy</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The roots of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/6/7e6ef5d8664f1952ed7e68b9b5b394c50efd1b55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^3 + 2x^2 - x + 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"133\" height=\"18\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/c/0ec2b6f850a38c18bff9b2d860b248982102966e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p, q,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"31\" height=\"11\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/9/279a83610a37e3f83bb8d2544695241ca8066834.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> What is the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/8/938ecf6869b053c8335864493848733a3f242e2e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(p^2 + 4)(q^2 + 4)(r^2 + 4)?\\]\" width=\"191\" height=\"20\" /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/4/f441a79a5a6e68517c8bcffe02a171db5220432b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 64 \\qquad \\textbf{(B) } 75 \\qquad \\textbf{(C) } 100 \\qquad \\textbf{(D) } 125 \\qquad \\textbf{(E) } 144$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"428\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>You can factor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/c/1ac8b8de3e896514ed4729443fa1cb7c8e412873.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(p^2 + 4)(q^2 + 4)(r^2 + 4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"187\" height=\"21\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/4/4f4ce24920c10b31207a7fe00ad1b0785eba7515.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(p+2i)(p-2i)(q+2i)(q-2i)(r+2i)(r-2i)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"365\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>For any polynomial <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" />, you can create a new polynomial <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/e/e0e54c792c30b47c2e8ae11444119f389800e963.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x+a)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"69\" height=\"20\" />, which will have roots that instead have the value <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> subtracted.\n</p><p>Substituting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/4/b74dc599f235adf580f9863e094d104755f07054.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x-2i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/c/e5cf9076da4ac529bc75f24c52a3986a6ca8c5b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+2i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"15\" /> into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> for the first polynomial, gives you <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/3/833307d2f0315ef418b0d1303830743c9b18e237.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10i-5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"58\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/c/58c461f3c078eb1f4399feb4b837fd47dcaae47b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-10i-5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"72\" height=\"15\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> for both equations. Multiplying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/3/833307d2f0315ef418b0d1303830743c9b18e237.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10i-5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"58\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/c/58c461f3c078eb1f4399feb4b837fd47dcaae47b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-10i-5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"72\" height=\"15\" /> together gives you <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/3/3032c853781d23c6e3a6029090f221fe752cd2a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }125}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"76\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>-ev2028\n</p><p>~Latex by eevee9406\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/1/891f251c2d8e7a5debda62b8e219f5afd9f26460.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = x^3 + 2x^2 - x + 3 = (x - p)(x - q)(x - r) = -(p - x)(q - x)(r - x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"589\" height=\"21\" />. Then\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/2/80269c5398c2d96c0422e71a3c068f8140c655f0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(p^2 + 4)(q^2 + 4)(r^2 + 4)=(p+2i)(p-2i)(q+2i)(q-2i)(r+2i)(r-2i)=f(2i)f(-2i).\\]\" width=\"621\" height=\"20\" />\nWe find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/5/d15ad80ecf43d605c219023025f008bec05ad549.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(2i)=-8i-8-2i+3=-10i-5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"290\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/b/b9b8cb35b0063ba34247cee6670a7ff385b981bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(-2i)=8i-8+2i+3=10i-5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"276\" height=\"20\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/2/7e2fc78a939c96f946ae75cac17aad42be12362a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(2i)f(-2i)=(-5-10i)(-5+10i)=(-5)^2-(10i)^2=25+100=\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }125}.\\]\" width=\"585\" height=\"28\" />\n~eevee9406\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, denote that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/d/5fd7adfa7164625bc4556437c944b4fe9c65594f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[p+q+r=-2, pq+pr+qr=-1, pqr=-3\\]\" width=\"354\" height=\"15\" />\nThen we expand the expression\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/c/79c9797d0b2895f4ab088d5ff787d893c4eb7e3c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(p^2+4)(q^2+4)(r^2+4)\\]\" width=\"182\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/1/3217d6c2547f5ff7bf3821bb3c4d16e5ec4f6d32.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[=(pqr)^2+4((pq)^2+(pr)^2+(qr)^2)+4^2(p^2+q^2+r^2)+4^3\\]\" width=\"458\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/9/9892c5a6f5545bc6c5390b1e8035af2acac54d35.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[=(-3)^2+4((pq+pr+qr)^2-2pqr(p+q+r))+4^2((p+q+r)^2-2(pq+pr+qr))+4^3\\]\" width=\"591\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/4/1f47291e68d0412309c509a07f76311f3ab4fa6f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[=(-3)^2+4((-1)^2-2(-3)(-2))+4^2((-2)^2-2(-1))+4^3\\]\" width=\"463\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/d/74d1dee45a2a8fdd3f738d3c79ba8b068341582c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[=\\fbox{(D) 125}\\]\" width=\"86\" height=\"28\" />\n~lptoggled\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Newton.27s_Sums_and_Vieta.27s.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Newton's_Sums_and_Vieta's)\">Solution 4 (Newton's Sums and Vieta's)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Newton&#39;s Sums and Vieta&#39;s)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Expand the expression: \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/845e5bbfd832e6ae870dda0fc57827fae217b216.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(p^2 + 4)(q^2 + 4)(r^2 + 4) = (p^2q^2r^2) + 4(q^2r^2 + p^2r^2 + p^2q^2) + 16(p^2 + q^2 + r^2) + 64.\\]\" width=\"569\" height=\"20\" /> \n</p><p>By Vieta's we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/9/239949b07fcc54db6275a8443127c9e0696beef6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$pqr = -3.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"81\" height=\"17\" /> Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/4/654eb877e74bea28ea37f2d6b2cc6805406c7b86.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^2q^2r^2 = (-3)^2 = 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"153\" height=\"21\" />. We use Newton's Sums to quickly compute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f191dfa46db2fb2f678557694d767d37b5c8dbdf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^2 + q^2 + r^2:$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"105\" height=\"20\" /> \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/e/e0e9d5842c4e060db415bb6bc76e2c4f35a90d63.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[S_2 + 2S_1 + 2(-1) = 0\\]\" width=\"169\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>By Vieta's again, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/b/eab0671741335ed0260d2a2ba4b7f5ba6c1567a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_1 = p + q + r = -2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"163\" height=\"18\" /> which means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e5926a087acad6fb3d79d1c1d686a172fb040716.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_2 = p^2 + q^2 + r^2 = 6.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"176\" height=\"20\" /> \n</p><p>Now all we need is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/3/993193bb1695758ec50d6f65791eec7dbe1eb73c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q^2r^2 + p^2r^2 + p^2q^2.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"149\" height=\"20\" /> Vieta's also tells us that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/a/84a5730d44f953df8354474b9322402bf579962f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$pq + qr + pr = -1,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"152\" height=\"17\" /> so we can take this equation and square both sides: \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/b/fcbff7a8a3ad56b080e6ada6bbb0151443e596a2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(pq + qr + pr)^2 = q^2r^2 + p^2r^2 + p^2q^2 + 2(qpr^2 + q^2rp + p^2rq) = 1.\\]\" width=\"513\" height=\"20\" /> \n</p><p>We know <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/0/920f312355bd4bca7aa1fde903844133b430eb60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$pqr = -3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"17\" /> so we can substitute this in: \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/6/5f6cba9b8ef4560a96dd091b4bf37715039558b9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(pq + qr + pr)^2 = q^2r^2 + p^2r^2 + p^2q^2 -6(r + p + q) = 1.\\]\" width=\"437\" height=\"20\" /> \n</p><p>We also know <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/5/e45baa30a622a96bb6f375f010cc080e07a321af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p + q + r = -2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"120\" height=\"17\" />, which means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/bae6d0a75af49439c8d0364506160356a5799ef2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q^2r^2 + p^2r^2 + p^2q^2 = -11.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"206\" height=\"20\" /> \n</p><p><br />\nSo the answer is just <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/f/7af4047515eaa22bcf4b85fc4b787d53be4bd82c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9 + 4(-11) + 16(6) + 64 = \\boxed{125}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"261\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User:Grogg007\" title=\"User:Grogg007\">grogg007</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28Reduction_of_power.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(Reduction_of_power)\">Solution 5 (Reduction of power)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (Reduction of power)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The motivation for this solution is the observation that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/5/3c523c167a8cf2c984d18921ad87c856ea8447fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(p+c)(q+c)(r+c)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"161\" height=\"20\" /> is easy to compute for any constant c, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/9/ac9715492165a9aa2edd0ee4075b023710f5c06f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(p+c)(q+c)(r+c)=-f(-c)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"247\" height=\"20\" /> (*), where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> is the polynomial given in the problem. The idea is to transform the expression involving <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/3/833343d60e29fbb15f6c0fde986a56a6a17f95b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^2, q^2, r^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"20\" /> into one involving <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/6/48689d638ddca59030006d362cbd848607f63aa2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p, q, r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"11\" />.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is a root of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" />, \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/d/c4daf80abfd0a67f0bb85a4ce20a5db737ef72a1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[p^3+2p^2-p+3=0\\implies p^3+2p^2=p^2(p+2)=p-3,\\]\" width=\"439\" height=\"20\" />\nwhich gives us that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/1/ab1ff6abb891015559cd42d30a0b3c11e023044a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^2=\\frac{p-3}{p+2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"87\" height=\"42\" />. Then\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/2/c12fe14efb123838c1bb7f074053fc3796618fad.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[p^2+4=\\frac{p-3}{p+2} + 4 = \\frac{5p+5}{p+2}=5\\cdot \\frac{p+1}{p+2}.\\]\" width=\"321\" height=\"41\" />\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> are also roots of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" />, the same analysis holds, so\n</p><p>\\begin{align*}\n(p^2 + 4)(q^2 + 4)(r^2 + 4)&amp;= \\left(5\\cdot \\frac{p+1}{p+2}\\right)\\left(5\\cdot \\frac{q+1}{q+2}\\right)\\left(5\\cdot \\frac{r+1}{r+2}\\right)\\\\\n&amp;= 125 \\frac{(p+1)(q+1)(r+1)}{(p+2)(q+2)(r+2)}\\\\\n&amp;= 125 \\frac{-f(-1)}{-f(-2)} \\\\\n&amp;= 125\\cdot 1\\\\\n&amp;=\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }125}.\n\\end{align*}\n</p><p>(*) This is because \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/7/e8741e44d21483bf85c8c06fec8f80e2293a646a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(p+c)(r+c)(q+c)=(-1)^3(-c-p)(-c-r)(-c-q)=-f(-c),\\]\" width=\"518\" height=\"20\" />\nsince\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/1/23180bab3619f839043b69c4871dacb9550ab37e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(x)=(x-p)(x-q)(x-r)\\]\" width=\"224\" height=\"18\" />\nfor all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p>~tsun26\n~KSH31415 (final step and clarification)\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_6_.28Cheesing_it_out.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6_(Cheesing_it_out)\">Solution 6 (Cheesing it out)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6 (Cheesing it out)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Expanding the expression\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/f/90f16bd076a2fd7f53cf631859fa19005453e735.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(p^2 + 4)(q^2 + 4)(r^2 + 4)\\]\" width=\"182\" height=\"20\" />\ngives us\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/9/ff955ca53318ea7e0e1f365f20750ca019c326f9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(pqr)^2+4p^2q^2+4p^2r^2+4q^2r^2+16p^2+16q^2+16r^2+64\\]\" width=\"449\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Notice that everything other than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/e/4def0e5245d9897161141a7d32f9914f58089e81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(pqr)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"50\" height=\"21\" /> is a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Solving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/e/4def0e5245d9897161141a7d32f9914f58089e81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(pqr)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"50\" height=\"21\" /> using vieta's formulas, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/2/2f2659fe9ff33c527f54d2ad69e9ba6dd084a3d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\pmod4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"18\" />, the answer should be as well. The only answer that is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/2/2f2659fe9ff33c527f54d2ad69e9ba6dd084a3d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\pmod4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/3/3032c853781d23c6e3a6029090f221fe752cd2a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }125}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"76\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~callyaops\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_7\">Solution 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/b/81be55f40fa0991a37ece629f846286aa00d8442.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = x^2 + 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"85\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/8/4a83140671c4b104329288cb4aa277b51a20ff95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x =\\pm \\sqrt{y - 4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"109\" height=\"24\" />. Substitute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/8/cc8cb25362f40813c102618d6bda122d3b644a45.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\sqrt{y - 4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"95\" height=\"24\" /> into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/9/c99c579d55128a921880876633f53b3e0544d400.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^3 + 2x^2 - x + 3 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"166\" height=\"18\" /> (It is same for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/4/474f1888b0bea9d84446a4fb3ef78bef3638f05d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = -\\sqrt{y - 4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"109\" height=\"24\" /> because the squares in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/c/1ac8b8de3e896514ed4729443fa1cb7c8e412873.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(p^2 + 4)(q^2 + 4)(r^2 + 4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"187\" height=\"21\" />)\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/4/484920a59fcd22266815c9e6bef3c1f88b6aee91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\sqrt{y - 4})^3 + 2(\\sqrt{y - 4})^2 - \\sqrt{y - 4} + 3 = 0 \\implies (y - 5)^2(y - 4) = (-2y + 5)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"616\" height=\"24\" /> whose constant is 125\n</p><p>according to Vieta's theorem, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/c/cac87e18b6e9195c78e6c898ff526cdc1681b533.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_1y_2y_3 = 125$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"102\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/a/e8aa5eb8305f0e5248e15195da686398e048aefc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_1y_2y_3 = 125 \\implies (x_1^2 + 4)(x_2^2 + 4)(x_3^2 + 4) = 125 \\implies (p^2 + 4)(q^2 + 4)(r^2 + 4) = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }125}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"727\" height=\"30\" />. \n</p><p>~JiYang\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution.2C_Fast.2C_Quick.2C_Easy.21\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution,_Fast,_Quick,_Easy!\">Video Solution, Fast, Quick, Easy!</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution, Fast, Quick, Easy!\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/g4xdfcFgwGo\">https://youtu.be/g4xdfcFgwGo</a> \n</p><p>~MathKatana\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_-_MaffyTaffy\">Video Solution - MaffyTaffy</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution - MaffyTaffy\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/Qyno5iqX_Jw\">https://youtu.be/Qyno5iqX_Jw</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12A\" title=